    <!-- ===== Per-brand background-keep tips ===== -->
    <!-- Each tip body uses "  •  " (NBSP + bullet + NBSP) at line starts so
         Compose renders as compact bullet rows. Separated by \n\n for
         paragraph spacing. These cover ONLY per-brand extras — anything the
         reliability checklist already handles (notifications, exact alarm,
         full-screen, battery-unrestricted) is intentionally left out. -->

    <string tools:ignore="MissingTranslation" name="setup_oem_keep_pixel">No extra Pixel setup is normally needed.\n\n  •  If Do Not Disturb is on, make sure alarms are allowed in that mode.</string>
    <string tools:ignore="MissingTranslation" name="setup_oem_keep_samsung">Samsung may move unused apps into Sleeping or Deep sleeping apps, which restricts alarms and foreground services.\n\n  •  Settings → Battery → Background usage limits → Never sleeping apps → add GT Wake.\n  •  Make sure GT Wake is not listed under Sleeping apps or Deep sleeping apps.\n  •  If watch sync is late, add Huawei Health to Never sleeping apps too.</string>
    <string tools:ignore="MissingTranslation" name="setup_oem_keep_xiaomi">If alarms are late on Xiaomi / HyperOS, check background autostart.\n\n  •  Settings → Apps → Permissions → Background autostart → GT Wake → On.\n  •  If available, allow background activity for GT Wake.</string>
    <string tools:ignore="MissingTranslation" name="setup_oem_keep_oneplus">If alarms are late on OxygenOS, check the app\'s battery settings.\n\n  •  Settings → Battery → More settings → App battery management → GT Wake.\n  •  Allow foreground/background activity for overnight alarm testing.</string>
    <string tools:ignore="MissingTranslation" name="setup_oem_keep_huawei">Huawei phones can block background launch unless you manage the app manually.\n\n  •  Phone Manager → App launch → GT Wake → Manage manually.\n  •  Turn on Auto-launch, Secondary launch, and Run in background.\n  •  Do the same for Huawei Health if watch sync is unreliable.</string>
    <string tools:ignore="MissingTranslation" name="setup_oem_keep_other">If your phone has a Phone Manager / Security app, look for Protected apps, Autostart, or Background activity.\n\n  •  Add GT Wake there only if alarms are late after the required checks pass.</string></resources>
